==English==

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|sg=[[electric]] [[charge]]}}

# {{physics}} the [[static]] electric [[energy]] of a charged body; the quantity of unbalanced positive or negative ions in or on an object; measured in [[coulomb]]s
# {{physics}} a [[quantum number]] of some [[subatomic particle]]s which determines their [[electromagnetic]] [[interaction]]s; by [[convention]] the [[electron]] has an electric charge of -1, the [[proton]] +1 and [[quark]]s have [[fractional]] charge

